Oxford's OCHS work makes the OCR point particularly clear: their team reports a Transkribus model trained on 500+ manuscript pages reaching expected accuracy above 97% on much of its suitable Sanskrit collection. Generic manuscript transcription is going to improve extremely rapidly. ([Theology Oxford][10]) eScriptorium already provides an HTR/OCR production pipeline and REST API. ([eScriptorium][11])

**You gain almost nothing from winning that engineering race yourself.**

