# The architecture should therefore be aggressively federated

This is the part I'd give the build agents.

Everything entering Pāṭala goes through one invariant boundary:

```text
EXTERNAL WORLD
     │
     ├── Gyan Bharatam
     ├── PANDiT
     ├── SAMHiTA
     ├── Muktabodha
     ├── GRETIL
     ├── SARIT
     ├── DCS
     ├── BDRC
     ├── Crossref
     ├── OpenAlex
     └── future unknown thing
             │
             ▼
       SOURCE CONNECTOR
             │
             ▼
      RawObservation
       + Artifact
       + External ID
             │
             ▼
      ExtractionActivity
             │
             ▼
     CandidateAssertions
             │
             ▼
      IDENTITY RESOLVER
             │
             ▼
       Pāṭala Entities
      / Assertions /
       Evidence Uses
             │
             ▼
     Adjudication Events
             │
             ▼
     CURRENT PROJECTION
```

**Every provider remains a provider.**

Don't turn a PANDiT record directly into `Work`.

Instead:

```text
PANDiT record 12345
        ↓
RawObservation PT...
        ↓
PanditExtractor/v3
        ↓
assertion:
  external_record_12345
  claims title X

assertion:
  external_record_12345
  claims author Y

identity assertion:
  record probably refers to PTW_...
```

That tiny distinction is the difference between:

**“Pāṭala copied PANDiT.”**

and

**“Pāṭala knows what PANDiT said.”**

The second survives everything.

