# Then make every external capability a replaceable tool

For Sanskrit text analysis, don't make one sacred pipeline.

Use a capability registry:

```text
CAPABILITY: sanskrit.segment

providers:
    vidyut
    sanskrit_heritage
    byt5_sanskrit
    translist
    patala_agent

CAPABILITY: manuscript.htr

providers:
    transkribus
    escriptorium_kraken
    gyan_bharatam_if_available
    future_model

CAPABILITY: bibliography.resolve

providers:
    crossref
    openalex

CAPABILITY: scholar.resolve

providers:
    orcid

CAPABILITY: institution.resolve

providers:
    ror
```

DCS/Sanskrit Heritage alignment research has already demonstrated why multiple independent linguistic systems are useful: disagreements themselves can identify errors and produce better gold data. ([arXiv][12])

That idea maps perfectly onto Pāṭala.

**Tools don't become truth. Their outputs become observations.**

This is a huge architectural principle.

