# Manuscripts: IIIF + Mirador, immediately

This one is almost a total no-brainer.

IIIF already defines interoperable presentation of cultural objects and annotation over canvases. ([IIIF][14]) Mirador already gives you multi-manuscript zooming, comparison and annotations. ([Mirador][15])

So a Pāṭala manuscript page should effectively be:

```text
Pāṭala identity/evidence
        +
IIIF Manifest
        +
Mirador viewer
        +
Pāṭala annotations
```

Your `TextAnchor/ImageAnchor` remains internal.

Adapter:

```text
Pāṭala anchor
     ↓
W3C Web Annotation
     ↓
IIIF target
```

Exactly as your hardening note proposes.

