# Texts: TEI + DTS, not a proprietary reader protocol

SARIT already provides the proof case for Sanskrit TEI and freely available encoded corpora. ([CLARIAH-AT][5]) DTS explicitly exists to expose text collections as machine-actionable interoperable resources, with collection/navigation/document endpoints. ([DTS API][16])

Internally keep your own representation.

Externally:

```text
GET Pāṭala text
→ JSON API

GET Pāṭala text as TEI
→ TEI

navigate passages
→ DTS

manuscript surfaces
→ IIIF
```

That is interoperability without ontology capture.

