# Scholar infrastructure: don't build ORCID/OpenReview again

This is another place your earlier vision can become much cheaper.

ORCID = scholar identity.

ROR = institution identity.

Crossref/OpenAlex = modern scholarly output graph.

OpenReview = mechanics of proposals/reviews/workflows.

OpenReview exposes a REST API around people, groups, submissions, reviews, assignments and workflow patterns. ([OpenReview][17])

Pāṭala's novel layer isn't “we invented reviewing.”

It's:

```text
Scholar attestation
      ↓
specific Pāṭala Assertion
      ↓
specific EvidenceUse
      ↓
specific Passage/Artifact
      ↓
specific scholarly state
```

Then the scholar's identity may resolve to ORCID.

That creates the “scholar stamp of approval” system you've been circling without inventing an entire scholarly identity ecosystem yourself.

