# I would actually change your execution order slightly

Your H0–H18 hardening sequence is fundamentally right.

But **before massive data ingestion**, I would add one concrete integration milestone:

> **Make the same Pāṭala Work emerge from five independent providers without making any provider canonical.**

Pick a famous text.

Ingest:

```text
PANDiT record
Muktabodha/GRETIL e-text
SARIT/DCS linguistic representation if available
OpenAlex/Crossref scholarship
a manuscript/IIIF source
```

Preserve every raw observation.

Resolve them to one PTW ID.

Expose every disagreement.

Generate a Work projection.

Then destroy Postgres and replay it.

If that works, you've demonstrated the actual product.

Not merely future-proof event sourcing.

You have demonstrated:

**Pāṭala can sit above the fragmented Sanskrit internet and make it coherent without swallowing it.**

That is the test I'd put immediately after your archival spine work and before dumping thousands/millions of records into it.

